ying to break down those  walls  but there's a couple of quirks in  netrunner that make it just so much more  creative  unique and fun to play for one the  neuron is not always going to turn up  this card and find agendas in these  servers  no the corporation can lay devastating  traps for the runner destroying their  hand getting rid of their cards dealing  brain damage so part of the way that you  play as the corp is trying to mislead  and bluff them as to where you're  keeping your agendas  where you're trying to score points so  they don't know where to attack  and because the corporation gets to  place their cards face  down the runner when they're coming up  against them doesn't always know what  they're gonna find  and then they turn it over and oh no i  can't stop but i haven't got the tools i  haven't got the programs and it does  three net damage so for the runner  it's a game of hedging your bids trying  to figure out now's the time to strike  you're never going to be able to respond  to every kind device they can put down  but you've got to run before the  corporation gets too  powerful mechanically netrunner is  really creative but i think that what  sets it apart from other card games  like magic gathering even more is that  you are  much less dependent on the cards that  you draw  and that's because the setup that you  create the cards that you  get down on the board cannot be so  easily destroyed by your opponent in one  or two turns a plan that you build up to  for ages and it's just over it's just  gone  seeing a massive monster come out on the  board can mean game over in a couple of  turns  but equally your massive monster that  you paid everything to get  can be murdered with a really cheap card  and that's just  your whole plan gone netrunner is not  nearly as temperamental the ice that the  corporation puts out cannot be destroyed  by the netrunner and the netrunner's  programs and hardware and resources are  pretty  hard for the corporation to destroy it  won't happen very often in a game  you're not really waiting for a big  powerful card to win you the game  in other words because plans are not  dependent on  and cannot be so easily undone by chance  netrunner is a game that's a lot more  dependent on your planning  and your skill now to be fair this does  mean the netrunner is probably a slower  paced  game than you might be used to you know  it doesn't have that constant  boom and collapse that comes from cards  rapidly entering the battlefield and  exiting the battlefield and exciting  moments it's and that is exciting don't  get me wrong but it's not what this  game is so much about uh there is  instead this  rising tension across the game you know  where choosing your moment is really  important it's crucial  if i make a run now he won't put down  another piece of ice to defend that  agenda  but i might not have enough to get  through whatever that card is  at its heart near runner is a game about  bluffing and choosing your moment to  strike  and i think that's a wonderful shift  away from other card games where it's  just about  knowing and learning a million key words  i'm about to win i attack your monster  it's weak right now aha  but it's got bedazzle what does that  mean it means i do 10 damage without  paying for it ugh  well how was i meant to know that it  doesn't even say it on the card yeah  anyway i attack you and i win now  the slow pace doesn't mean that there  aren't those same aha i got you moments  because there are there  are great feedback loops for the runner  and the corp when the runner gets  through the ice and  manages to steal an agenda or destroy a  valuable card and it's  incredibly satisfying when the runner  spends all of their money and all of  their actions are  trying to get through your ice and then  suddenly it's a trap  and they get damaged they lose all their  cards that's also really great but those  are things you build to over several  turns  gradually they're not something that  you'll keep in your hand and then throw  down on the table so much  this is all complimented by something  that i find pretty important in games  and that's  theme i like games that disguise the  maths that i am doing  and netrunner it totally succeeds at  this  the designers went out of their way to  use terms that really reinforce this  cyberpunk  theme you know they they kind of get you  to think about the stuff that you're  doing  in cyberpunk terms they took a lot of  the words by the way from william  gibson's  neuromancer a book that i reviewed and  you can go watch up in the  corner right now or after the video it's  stuff like ice  icebreaker stack rig netrunner the names  of  quite a number of the cards i actually  read and i was like hey i recognized  that  so it is really a gorgeous game  thematically and i really like that  but i think even more so what makes  netrunner so immersive as a game is the  asymmetricality again between the runner  and the corp  because the different styles of play  really embody the differences  between them in the world itself the big  lumbering corporation only gets three  actions per turn because it's a  bigger slower entity while the  independent  fast thinking netrunner gets four the  runner can lose when they take brain  damage and die because they're hooking  their mind into this machine  the corporation on the other end is  trying to track the runner down they're  trying to put these tracking tokens  on the other player because they live in  secret they're trying to find to them  i will admit that there is one element  of the gameplay that is  weirdly unfamatic and that's that it's  oddly enough  easier to get rich as the net runner  than it is as the corporation  and that's kind of a consequence of how  the game works if the corp also had a  crap ton of money then there would be no  way for the netrunner to win  but it is still kind of strange and i  still plan to go i wish there was a way  for the court to be the one with the  money it feels weird when you win as the  netrunner because you outspend the  corporation i mean you should really win  through subterfuge shouldn't you  however it does need to be said that  netrunner is  not an even-handed game it is harder to  play as the corporation than it is to  play  as the runner it's harder to learn the  strategy for playing the court  when and which cards you should play the  runner has the advantage in the early  game because the corp can't defend  everything that they need to protect  and in the late game they can break  through almost anything you have a  narrow window of victory in the middle  of the game  now this isn't a bad thing by itself but  it can  feel unfair especially when you're  learning and it  magnifies any skill differences between  you  and the other player that you're playing  up against and some people do like games  where it's always going to be  even-handed no matter which faction you  choose to play with especially if you  like one play style more but it's always  harder to win  that would kind of suck but i think  just like in this monster  psy not every faction is you know  equally powerful there are clearly a  couple of factions in scythe one of the  most popular games in the world  which are better than others and that's  okay  you know it creates a different strategy  it creates different challenge and it's  just important to recognize  that winning as the corporation is more  of an achievement in many ways than  running as  than winning as the runner connected to  this is the problem of steamrolling i  have noticed that if  one side gets a car that gets them a lot  of money early in the game then they do  tend to win a lot more easily because  the only way to stop them is by spending  money and it just creates the cycle  where you know you'll go up against them  you'll fail they'll get more money  you'll get less  and then the game's over from that point  but i mean that is