ich i appreciate that a lot of other  people really do  like um and that's okay so if you are a  dick builder you can create your own  destiny runner but  it's not really the same as you might be  used to i think netrunner is for people  who  like card games but want one that allows  them to plan out and deliver on their  plans  more to see what they build up pay off  building a more elaborate economy and  strategy  than magic or hearthstone allow you to  at the moment  and who don't want you know expensive  plans blown apart  in a single turn by a cheap car that you  could not have seen coming  it's probably not for the people who  love that fast-paced  bombastic you know throwing cards down  getting them on the board getting them  off board  that instant cycle that a lot of people  really love if you like that then  maybe not for you we're being flexible  and having backup plan after backup  planner for backup plan  is key to winning it is for people who  love the cyberpunk genre and want to see  a game that truly replicates its themes  i think it should be pretty obvious that  i totally recommend it personally but i  would love to hear your thoughts on the  game and your thoughts on magic and  hearthstone and other games like  whether you feel i'm at all being fair  to them  let me know down below hope you enjoyed  this review  stay nerdy and i will see you in the  future
 

